+subnormals kept: rp_fadd_asm is IEEE bit for bit), so the compare of the
+two sides on their bits gives RP_Ge0 and RP_Lt0's answers. 1: a < d, 0:
+a >= d, -1: an operand is a NaN or an infinity (the caller subtracts, as
+before). The value itself is made only where it is used (a straddled
+node's crossing), the same operations in the same order.
