+/*
+Kit 90 (R324, run 100: RP_LPlane 3.0% and RP_LightPointFix 3.8% of the
+play; the hot windows are the float-bit reads RP_LFix makes at every visit,
+four for each turned plane met and eight for each surface tried).
+Iterate (rule 0): Quake, GoldSrc and Xash walk mnode_t (52 bytes) and its
+float plane (20 more, elsewhere) in floats; kit 79 read those floats' bits
+into 16.16 at every visit (no table, no memory). Ours reads them once a
+map: a packed 24-byte light node (the plane's 16.16 distance and 2^30
+normal, the children as node numbers, the surface range) and each
+texinfo's lightmap vectors in 16.16 (Xash makes every surface's from its
+texinfo alone; checked surface by surface as the table is made). The walk
+makes the same integer sums of the same numbers in the same order, so the
